  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">218472 FY21 WFP CLOSED Nsele CBT Phase 2 DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For expenditure data on these and all other World Vision DRC projects, please see the related activity, published by World Vision International (US-EIN-95-3202116-CD)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Part of WVUK WFP FY22 portfolio of projects 

The overall objective of this intervention is mainly to mitigate against the negative socio-economic impact of COVID-19 on the targeted children and households of the Nsele population. The intervention also aims to provide support to the Government of the DRC to establish the basis for a national social protection system, which can be adapted for use by intervening agencies, and the government. 

                

The project intends to cushion the affected population against further negative social and economic impacts posed by the COVID-19 pandemic. 12,000 households from Nsele Commune and surroundings with an estimated population of 72,000 beneficiaries are set to benefit from the intervention.</narrative>
  </description>
